// macros/Say.fol — package source file in package "macros"
// Spec: language-ref.md > Macros
//
// The basic macro form: build a syntax tree with co.macro.quote and return it.
// A macro is a primary declaration, so it gets its own source file.
//
// The name is explicit: filename inference works through `declaration-name`,
// but a macro is an `annotated-function-primary` whose name position is
// `function-name = identifier | lifecycle-name`, and a lone `_` is never an
// identifier.

_ co.lang.unit = {
@co.dap.macro
Say()->() = {
    this.return co.macro.quote({
        co.out.println("Line 1");
        co.out.println("Line 2");
    });
}
}
